<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seville</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seville is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalquivir">Guadalquivir</a> River. It served as a capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>, where the Almohads built the great mosque whose minaret survives as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giralda">Giralda</a>. It later became the monopoly port for Spanish trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, as accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> note.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seville.jpg" alt="Seville" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ingo Mehling · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sevilla_Cathedral_-_Southeast.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
